# tools/baremetal/wg_peer_config.qz — operator-supplied WireGuard peer
# config for the Quartz unikernel.
#
# Default body: empty stub. The unikernel boots with no peers in its WG
# table, so any inbound MSG_INITIATION is dropped (no peer matches the
# decoded static_pub). HTTP/UDP-echo paths are unaffected.
#
# The `quake baremetal:qemu_wg_interop` task replaces this file with a
# generated version that hardcodes a peer's static_pub + (optional) PSK
# + allowed_ips for the duration of the interop test, then restores the
# default. The generated body uses the wg_device_add_peer API directly.

def wg_demo_install_peer(): Void
  # No peer configured — see file header for the override mechanism.
end
